# The ledger of `mongodb`: what a program does with a MongoDB server,
# measured against the official drivers: Go's
# `go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2` v2.10.0 (`go doc -all` of `mongo`,
# `mongo/options`, `mongo/readpref`, `mongo/readconcern` and
# `mongo/writeconcern`, fetched into the scratch folder on 2026-11-18),
# Rust's `mongodb` crate 3.10.1 (its rustdoc built in the scratch folder the
# same day: `all.html` and the methods of `Client`, `Database`, `Collection`,
# `Cursor`, `SessionCursor`, `ClientSession`, `ClientOptions`, `IndexModel`
# and `error::Error`) and Python's pymongo 4.20.0 (`dir()` of `MongoClient`,
# `Database`, `Collection`, `Cursor`, `CommandCursor`, `ClientSession`,
# `errors`, `operations`, `results` and `uri_parser`).
#
# The live runs, on 2026-11-18, reached MongoDB 7.0.48 (`mongo:7`, 1.14 GB,
# in the container `rebel-mongodb` of this Mac) as a one-member replica set
# `rs0` with authentication on and TLS allowed on one port, its certificate
# `tls`'s test certificate for `localhost`. The expected values of the unit
# tests were observed: pymongo 4.20 read the connection strings and answered
# SASLprep; Python computed RFC 7677's SCRAM exchange and MongoDB's SHA-1
# digest; RFC 3454's tables were read from Python 3.15's `stringprep`. The
# SCRAM exchange, SASLprep and the tables are the package `scram`'s since
# 2026-11-20 (the coherence review's D15), and their tests went with them.

capability mongodb/connect  a client connected by its options or a connection string
  heroes  mongodb.connect, mongodb.options, mongodb.parse_url, mongodb.Options, mongodb.Host, mongodb.Client, mongodb.DEFAULT_PORT
  go      Connect, options.Client, ClientOptions.ApplyURI, ClientOptions.SetHosts, ClientOptions.SetAuth, Client
  rust    Client::with_uri_str, Client::with_options, ClientOptions::parse, ClientOptions::builder, Client
  python  MongoClient, uri_parser.parse_uri, uri_parser.parse_host, uri_parser.split_hosts, uri_parser.split_options, uri_parser.parse_userinfo, uri_parser.validate_options, MongoClient.HOST, MongoClient.PORT
  note    an unknown option is refused, as pymongo refuses it (Go and Rust ignore one); the options of a pool, a monitor and server selection's timing are read and have no effect

capability mongodb/srv  servers and options found by DNS for mongodb+srv://
  heroes  mongodb.connect, mongodb.Options.srv_name, mongodb.Options.srv_service_name, mongodb.Options.srv_max_hosts
  go      ClientOptions.ApplyURI with mongodb+srv, SetSRVServiceName, SetSRVMaxHosts
  rust    ClientOptions::parse with mongodb+srv, srv_service_name, srv_max_hosts
  python  MongoClient with mongodb+srv, srvServiceName, srvMaxHosts
  note    SRV and TXT asked of the system's resolver through `dns`; a server outside the name's domain and a second TXT record are refused; srvMaxHosts takes the first records, where the specification draws them at random. Unrun live: no DNS server here names this machine's server

capability mongodb/tls  the connection secured by TLS, the server's certificate checked
  heroes  mongodb.Security, mongodb.Options.security
  go      ClientOptions.SetTLSConfig
  rust    options::Tls, TlsOptions
  python  tls, tlsCAFile, ssl
  note    run live over `tls`; `tlsInsecure`, `tlsAllowInvalidCertificates` and `tlsAllowInvalidHostnames` are refused, `unsupported`

capability mongodb/tls-client-certificate  a client certificate offered, and X.509's login
  heroes  pending: `tls` offers no client certificate
  go      ClientOptions.SetTLSConfig with Certificates, MONGODB-X509
  rust    TlsOptions::cert_key_file_path, AuthMechanism::MongoDbX509
  python  tlsCertificateKeyFile, tlsCertificateKeyFilePassword, MONGODB-X509

capability mongodb/auth-scram  a login by SCRAM-SHA-256 or SCRAM-SHA-1, negotiated, the password prepared by SASLprep
  heroes  mongodb.connect, mongodb.Mechanism, mongodb.Options.username, mongodb.Options.password, mongodb.Options.auth_source
  go      options.Credential, ClientOptions.SetAuth
  rust    options::Credential, AuthMechanism::ScramSha1, AuthMechanism::ScramSha256
  python  username, password, authSource, authMechanism
  note    run live against users of each mechanism, a SASLprep password (U+2168 logs in as IX), a wrong password and a forced mechanism the user lacks, on 2026-11-18; the server's signature is checked and an iteration count below 4096 refused. The exchange and SASLprep are `scram`'s since 2026-11-20, and MongoDB's SHA-1 digest stays here: a password SASLprep refuses is sent as its bytes now, the server answering, where it failed `invalid` before the login until then (`scram.ledger`'s `scram/password`)

capability mongodb/auth-plain  a login by SASL PLAIN, LDAP's proxy
  heroes  mongodb.Mechanism.sasl_plain
  go      options.Credential with PLAIN
  rust    AuthMechanism::Plain
  python  authMechanism=PLAIN
  note    unrun live: this server has no LDAP; the message is SASL's own, `\0user\0password`

capability mongodb/auth-other  logins by Kerberos, AWS and OIDC
  heroes  pending: GSSAPI needs the system's Kerberos library, which no package binds; MONGODB-AWS needs Signature Version 4 and STS, which `s3` holds a layer above; MONGODB-OIDC needs a callback driven by the program and HTTP
  go      GSSAPI, MONGODB-AWS, MONGODB-OIDC, Credential.OIDCMachineCallback, Credential.OIDCHumanCallback
  rust    AuthMechanism::Gssapi, AuthMechanism::MongoDbAws, AuthMechanism::MongoDbOidc, oidc
  python  GSSAPI, MONGODB-AWS, MONGODB-OIDC, auth_oidc_shared

capability mongodb/handshake  the server greeted, the client's name and the server's limits learned
  heroes  mongodb.connect, mongodb.server_of, mongodb.ServerInfo, mongodb.Options.app_name
  go      ClientOptions.SetAppName, Client.AppendDriverInfo
  rust    ClientOptions::app_name, ClientOptions::driver_info, Client::append_metadata
  python  appname, driver, MongoClient.append_metadata, MongoClient.server_info, MongoClient.address, MongoClient.is_primary, MongoClient.is_mongos
  note    `hello`, and the legacy `isMaster` where the server knows no `hello`; the server's version is `run_command` of `buildInfo`

capability mongodb/server-selection  the server chosen by read preference and replica set
  heroes  mongodb.ReadPreference, mongodb.Options.read_preference, mongodb.Options.replica_set, mongodb.Options.direct
  go      readpref.Primary, readpref.PrimaryPreferred, readpref.Secondary, readpref.SecondaryPreferred, readpref.Nearest, readpref.ReadPref, SetReadPreference, SetReplicaSet, SetDirect
  rust    SelectionCriteria, ReadPreference, ClientOptions::repl_set_name, ClientOptions::direct_connection
  python  ReadPreference, read_preferences, replicaSet, directConnection, MongoClient.primary, MongoClient.secondaries, MongoClient.arbiters, MongoClient.nodes
  note    chosen once, at connect, the server that is not the one wanted naming the one that is; tags and maxStalenessSeconds are not read; run live (a secondary on a one-member set is `not_found`)

capability mongodb/monitor  servers watched in the background and a changed primary followed
  heroes  refused: a monitor is a thread sharing the client, and threads share nothing in this language; a client reconnects, choosing again, when a read or a retryable write loses its server
  go      the topology monitor, event.ServerMonitor
  rust    the topology monitor, event::sdam
  python  the topology monitor, MongoClient.topology_description

capability mongodb/pool  connections pooled and shared between threads
  heroes  refused: threads share nothing in this language, so a pool has no one to share with; a thread opens its own client
  go      SetMaxPoolSize, SetMinPoolSize, SetMaxConnIdleTime, SetMaxConnecting, Client.NumberSessionsInProgress
  rust    max_pool_size, min_pool_size, max_idle_time, max_connecting, Client::warm_connection_pool
  python  maxPoolSize, minPoolSize, maxIdleTimeMS, waitQueueTimeoutMS, maxConnecting

capability mongodb/close  a client closed, its session ended
  heroes  mongodb.close, mongodb.is_closed
  go      Client.Disconnect
  rust    Client::shutdown
  python  MongoClient.close

capability mongodb/timeouts  the time a connection and each reply may take
  heroes  mongodb.Options.connect_timeout_ms, mongodb.Options.socket_timeout_ms, mongodb.set_timeout
  go      ClientOptions.SetConnectTimeout, ClientOptions.SetTimeout, SetServerSelectionTimeout
  rust    ClientOptions::connect_timeout, ClientOptions::server_selection_timeout
  python  connectTimeoutMS, socketTimeoutMS, timeoutMS, pymongo.timeout
  note    a reply past its time ends the client, since its bytes may still come; `maxTimeMS` is a field of a command's options

